NEARS-1725 AC1 live violation — render-tree proof (emulator-5558, 1344x2992px @480dpi = 448dp width, EN, store "Fast Market" id=21, zone 2)

Store: Fast Market, ratingCount=5, reviewCommentCount=5 (also reproduced with reviewCommentCount=15 on "The Grill House (Abu Dhabi)")
Mobile (non-desktop) RatingWidget arm — pills Row lives inside Expanded(flex:2) column, NOT the full 448dp screen width.

RenderParagraph "5 Ratings":
  constraints: BoxConstraints(0.0<=w<=56.0, 0.0<=h<=Infinity)
  size: Size(51.8, 14.0)   <- single line, content-hugs, well under its 56dp cap

RenderParagraph "5 Reviews":
  constraints: BoxConstraints(0.0<=w<=54.0, 0.0<=h<=Infinity)
  size: Size(54.0, 28.0)   <- height doubled to 28.0 (2x the 14.0 single-line height) = WRAPPED TO 2 LINES, pinned exactly at its 54dp cap

uiautomator a11y bounds (independent confirmation):
  "5 Ratings" bounds=[114,723][270,765] height=42px (single line)
  "5 Reviews" bounds=[333,702][495,786] height=84px (exactly 2x — two lines)

Reproduced again on a second store (The Grill House (Abu Dhabi), id=47) with reviewCommentCount=15:
  "0 Ratings" bounds=[114,723][270,765] height=42px (single line)
  "15 Reviews" bounds=[333,702][495,786] height=84px (two lines)

This is the ORIGINAL reported defect (AC1: "both pills render single-line for typical counts... at
common phone widths") persisting live after the fix, on a real device at 448dp — a width the ticket's
own widget test suite (rating_pills_single_line_test.dart, AC1 group) never actually exercises with a
count pair this tight (it only asserts single-line at ratingCount=12/reviewCount=4, width=448). The
engineer's own header comment in that test file (finding #4) explicitly predicted this: "the reviews
pill's WRAP OUTCOME is unchanged from the pre-fix bug in any case that was actually tight" — this is
exactly that tight case, hit by perfectly typical single/double-digit counts, not a contrived edge case.

The mobile RatingWidget's pills Row lives inside Expanded(flex:2) of the outer [flex:2 | divider | flex:3]
Row, giving it a real per-pill Flexible cap of only ~54-56dp — far narrower than the 448dp the isolated
widget-test harness pumps the same width into (the harness wraps RatingWidget itself in a SizedBox(width:
448), which DOES reach the same flex:2 column layout — the gap is coverage of tight counts, not a
different code path).
